1
00:00:07,905 --> 00:00:13,123
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,383 --> 00:00:15,367
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:16,525 --> 00:00:19,150
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:24,660
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَّ

5
00:00:25,913 --> 00:00:35,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ with 400 Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, went out in a battle called Zaat Ar-Riqaah(ذات الرقاع).

6
00:00:36,843 --> 00:00:41,958
Now Riqaah(رقاع) means pieces of cloth, rags.

7
00:00:42,701 --> 00:00:45,679
And the Ghazwah(غزوة) was given this name for the following reason,

8
00:00:45,703 --> 00:00:48,065
Abu Musa Al-Asha'ari رضي الله عنه said;

9
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:51,906
We went with Rasool Allah ﷺ in a Ghazwa(غزوة),

10
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:55,956
and I was one of six men, who were sharing the same Camel.

11
00:00:56,863 --> 00:01:00,646
Meaning, if you have six people sharing a camel,

12
00:01:01,124 --> 00:01:06,368
you'll only get to ride, one sixth of the times and the rest of the time you're walking on foot.

13
00:01:06,838 --> 00:01:07,477
So he said;

14
00:01:07,622 --> 00:01:10,106
فَنَقِبَتْ قَدْمَايَ وَسَقِطَتْ اَظْفَارِيْ

15
00:01:10,469 --> 00:01:15,494
The skin of my feet was peeling off and my nails were falling down.

16
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:20,667
And we would wrap rags, pieces of cloth around our feet.

17
00:01:21,332 --> 00:01:27,865
So, this was pretty tough walking on rocks and hot sand and all of that and

18
00:01:28,492 --> 00:01:31,640
in those days they didn't have pretty good boots.

19
00:01:32,329 --> 00:01:34,797
So, they had to wrap these pieces of cloth around their feet.

20
00:01:35,424 --> 00:01:38,102
So, that was the name of that Ghazwa(غزوة), Zaat Ar-Riqaah(ذات الرقاع).

21
00:01:38,718 --> 00:01:43,467
The enemy fled, they didn't face off, the Muslims,

22
00:01:43,959 --> 00:01:47,395
but the Muslims were careful and alert.

23
00:01:48,202 --> 00:01:52,808
So, when they prayed, they prayed in a form that is called Salah-Tul-Khauf(صلاة الخوف),

24
00:01:53,019 --> 00:01:54,133
the Salah(صلاة) of fear.

25
00:01:55,454 --> 00:01:58,120
And this Salah(صلاة) is prescribed in Qur'an.

26
00:01:58,596 --> 00:02:01,834
It's in verse 102 Surat Tun Nissah(سورة النساء).

27
00:02:02,326 --> 00:02:03,630
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

28
00:02:03,787 --> 00:02:13,733
وَإِذَا كُنْتَ فِيهِمْ فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلَاةَ فَلْتَقُمْ طَائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ مَعَكَ

29
00:02:14,471 --> 00:02:22,723
 فَلْتَقُمْ طَائِفَةٌ مِنْهُمْ مَعَكَ وَلْيَأْخُذُوا أَسْلِحَتَهُمْ

30
00:02:23,238 --> 00:02:35,881
فَإِذَا سَجَدُوا فَلْيَكُونُوا مِنْ وَرَائِكُمْ وَلْتَأْتِ طَائِفَةٌ أُخْرَىٰ لَمْ يُصَلُّوا فَلْيُصَلُّوا مَعَكَ

31
00:02:36,678 --> 00:02:40,710
وَلْيَأْخُذُوا حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ ۗ

32
00:02:41,146 --> 00:02:52,763
وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ تَغْفُلُونَ عَنْ أَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَأَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيلُونَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَيْلَةً وَاحِدَةً ۚ

33
00:02:53,395 --> 00:03:06,792
وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِنْ كَانَ بِكُمْ أَذًى مِنْ مَطَرٍ أَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضَىٰ أَنْ تَضَعُوا أَسْلِحَتَكُمْ ۖ

34
00:03:07,464 --> 00:03:15,362
وَخُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْكَافِرِينَ عَذَابًا مُهِينًا ۝

35
00:03:15,767 --> 00:03:25,114
فَإِذَا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلَاةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ قِيَامًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِكُمْ ۚ

36
00:03:25,556 --> 00:03:32,098
And when you, i.e. the commander of an army are among them, and lead them in prayer,

37
00:03:32,632 --> 00:03:35,487
let a group of them stand in prayer with you

38
00:03:35,774 --> 00:03:37,543
and let them carry their arms.

39
00:03:37,919 --> 00:03:40,013
So, they're standing in their Salah(صلاة) with their arms.

40
00:03:41,188 --> 00:03:44,918
And when they have prostrated let them be in position behind you

41
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:50,039
and have the other group come forward, which has not yet prayed and let them pray with you.

42
00:03:50,515 --> 00:03:53,031
Taking precaution and carrying their arms,

43
00:03:53,571 --> 00:03:59,034
those who disbelieve wish that you would neglect your weapons and your baggage,

44
00:03:59,336 --> 00:04:03,018
 so they could come down upon you in one single attack.

45
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:08,334
If you are troubled by rain, or are ill for putting down your arms

46
00:04:08,374 --> 00:04:13,111
but take precaution, indeed Allah has prepared for the disbelievers humiliating punishment.

47
00:04:13,196 --> 00:04:14,734
So, the way this Salah(صلاة) is performed,

48
00:04:15,374 --> 00:04:16,138
there's two opinions.

49
00:04:16,178 --> 00:04:22,543
 One is that, one part of the army prays behind the Imam(امام), while the other parts of the army is guarding.

50
00:04:23,004 --> 00:04:25,688
So, this half that is praying with the Imam(امام)

51
00:04:26,403 --> 00:04:28,266
would pray with the Imam(امام) one Rak'ah(ركعة).

52
00:04:29,117 --> 00:04:35,227
And then the Imam(امام) would stand up for the second Rak'ah(ركعة), and would not move.

53
00:04:35,686 --> 00:04:38,657
While they would finish their second Rak'ah(ركعة) and give Salam(سلام),

54
00:04:39,134 --> 00:04:41,241
which means that they prayed with the Imam(امام) one Rak'ah(ركعة),

55
00:04:41,266 --> 00:04:42,530
and the Imam(امام) is now waiting.

56
00:04:42,839 --> 00:04:46,996
The next group, the group that was guarding with them step in

57
00:04:47,366 --> 00:04:49,901
and they would pray with the Imam(امام) second Rak'ah(ركعة)

58
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:54,201
and then they would finish their second Rak'ah(ركعة) alone.

59
00:04:54,883 --> 00:04:56,706
This one opinion, the other opinion is that

60
00:04:57,147 --> 00:05:01,442
the Imam(امام) leads the first half, in the two Rak'ah(ركعة).

61
00:05:02,012 --> 00:05:03,617
And then they make Salaam(سلام),

62
00:05:03,657 --> 00:05:07,705
and then the next group comes in and pray another two Rak'ah(ركعة) with the Imam(امام).

63
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:09,680
So, the Imam(امام) would end up praying four Rak'ah(ركعة),

64
00:05:09,933 --> 00:05:13,826
while each half of the army would have prayed two Rak'ah(ركعة).

65
00:05:14,325 --> 00:05:17,071
So these are the two opinions of how Salah-Tul-Khauf(صلاة الخوف) is performed.

66
00:05:17,837 --> 00:05:20,082
The lesson here to mention is the importance of Salaah(صلاة)

67
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:26,922
that even if you are afraid that the enemy might ambush you, you still have to pray.

68
00:05:27,606 --> 00:05:32,486
So, if this is the case with the ones, who are fighting in the path of Allah,

69
00:05:32,526 --> 00:05:36,022
who are afraid of death, they still have to pray the Salah(صلاة).

70
00:05:36,431 --> 00:05:39,591
What about somebody who has really nothing urgent

71
00:05:40,317 --> 00:05:42,977
and nevertheless they neglect the Salawaat(صلوات).

72
00:05:43,883 --> 00:05:51,438
See in Islam, every Ibadah(عبادة), there are conditions where you don't have to do it, except Salah(صلاة).

73
00:05:51,721 --> 00:05:54,417
So for example the poor, don't have to pay Zakaat(زكواة),

74
00:05:54,846 --> 00:05:56,673
the ill don't have to fast,

75
00:05:57,157 --> 00:06:01,716
the financially incapable doesn't have to make Hajj(حَجْ), and so on.

76
00:06:01,791 --> 00:06:04,761
This could go on with everybody Ibadaah(عبادة), except Salah(صلاة).

77
00:06:05,158 --> 00:06:07,713
You're not excused at all.

78
00:06:08,936 --> 00:06:11,533
No matter what, a Muslim has to pray.

79
00:06:12,179 --> 00:06:16,385
If you can pray standing up you pray sitting down you can sitting down, you lay down,

80
00:06:16,832 --> 00:06:18,588
laying down you move your head, you can't move your head,

81
00:06:18,612 --> 00:06:20,332
 you move your you can't move your finger,

82
00:06:20,356 --> 00:06:23,258
you blink with your eye.

83
00:06:24,005 --> 00:06:25,784
The point is, Salah(صلاة) needs to be done.

84
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:31,913
It must be done, and a Muslim is not excused from not praying.

85
00:06:33,293 --> 00:06:36,355
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed guards that night

86
00:06:36,485 --> 00:06:42,634
 and the two guards were Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) and Abbad Bin Bishr(عباد بن بشر).

87
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:47,610
So, they would alternate, Abbad Bin Bishr(عباد بن بشر) would take his turn.

88
00:06:47,904 --> 00:06:50,099
While Ammar(عمار) would sleep and then vice versa.

89
00:06:50,538 --> 00:06:54,508
So, while Ammar(عمار) was sleeping, Abbad(عباد) was, the one guarding.

90
00:06:55,029 --> 00:06:59,276
He occupied himself with Salah(صلاة), he started praying.

91
00:07:00,257 --> 00:07:02,775
And while he was reciting.

92
00:07:03,478 --> 00:07:06,651
One of the enemy shots an arrow at him.

93
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,147
But he didn't move.

94
00:07:09,847 --> 00:07:11,715
So, he shot another arrow to him,

95
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,528
he still didn't move, he shot the third arrow at him

96
00:07:14,937 --> 00:07:18,283
and then Abbad(عباد) woke up Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر).

97
00:07:19,049 --> 00:07:24,337
So when Ammar(عمار) woke up and saw that Abbad(عباد) has three arrows sticking out of his body.

98
00:07:24,377 --> 00:07:25,084
 He told him;

99
00:07:25,755 --> 00:07:27,668
سبحان الله، هَلْ لَا نَبَّهتَنِيْ

100
00:07:27,977 --> 00:07:30,358
Glory be to Allah, why didn't you wake me up.

101
00:07:31,027 --> 00:07:31,778
 He said;

102
00:07:32,013 --> 00:07:36,581
كُنْتُ فِيْ سُوْرَةٍ اَقْرَاُهَا فَلَمْ اُحِبْ أنْ اَقْطَعَهَا

103
00:07:36,942 --> 00:07:42,125
فَلَمَّا تَابَعَ الرَّمْيَ رَكَعْتُ فَأُرِيتُكَ، وَأيْمُ اللهِ، لَوْلاَ أَنْ أُضَيِّعَ ثَغْرًا

104
00:07:42,149 --> 00:07:47,332
أَمَرَنِي رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِحِفْظِهِ، لَقَطَعَ نَفْسِي قَبْلَ أَنْ أَقْطَعَهَا أَوْ أُنْفِذَهَا

105
00:07:47,721 --> 00:07:49,770
 He said: I was reciting a Surah(سورة),

106
00:07:50,005 --> 00:07:53,339
and I didn't want to stop until, I finish it.

107
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:57,580
But when he kept on firing arrows at me.

108
00:07:57,889 --> 00:07:59,055
I made the Rukooh(ركوع).

109
00:07:59,373 --> 00:08:01,782
And then I woke you up and In the name of Allah,

110
00:08:01,942 --> 00:08:06,938
if it wasn't for that I would have caused my responsibility.

111
00:08:07,486 --> 00:08:11,561
If I would have been considered to be neglectful of my responsibility,

112
00:08:12,307 --> 00:08:14,477
which was given to me by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

113
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:21,271
I would have rather died, then stop my Salah(صلاة), or I would have finished it.

114
00:08:22,424 --> 00:08:25,239
Now, this is an impressive story.

115
00:08:25,989 --> 00:08:29,722
You see how much he loved Qur'an, he didn't want to stop,

116
00:08:29,895 --> 00:08:33,162
 and you know these arrows are striking at him.

117
00:08:33,636 --> 00:08:37,157
And even though he's suffering all of that pain,

118
00:08:37,197 --> 00:08:42,242
he still has the concentration, and Khushoo(خشوع) in Salah(صلاة)

119
00:08:42,282 --> 00:08:46,413
to carry on reading the Ayat(آيات) of Qur'an and this is truly amazing.

120
00:08:46,999 --> 00:08:50,659
But this shows you the level of Eeman(ايمان) that these Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had.

121
00:08:51,415 --> 00:08:53,278
We also see here that he said;

122
00:08:53,656 --> 00:08:57,486
I didn't want to neglect the responsibility given to me by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

123
00:08:57,526 --> 00:09:00,839
so now he was weighing these two things,

124
00:09:00,879 --> 00:09:02,597
 one he wants to carry on with the Salah(صلاة).

125
00:09:02,637 --> 00:09:06,015
Number two, He is responsible for guarding the Muslims

126
00:09:06,055 --> 00:09:08,817
and he doesn't want them, to be attacked from his side.

127
00:09:09,198 --> 00:09:10,833
And this world that he used Thaghar(ثغر),

128
00:09:11,716 --> 00:09:12,887
Thaghar(ثغر) means hole.

129
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:20,340
 So, you can imagine as if there is this hole or this opening, which the enemy can come through.

130
00:09:20,721 --> 00:09:23,876
And he is responsible for that Thaghar(ثغر)

131
00:09:23,916 --> 00:09:26,491
 and this word repeats a lot in Arabic,

132
00:09:26,583 --> 00:09:30,943
you know that every Muslim is on a Thaghar(ثغر), every Muslim is at this opening

133
00:09:31,149 --> 00:09:34,617
and you don't want the enemy to approach the Ummah(امة) from your opening.

134
00:09:35,025 --> 00:09:40,493
We need to imagine ourselves as if every one of us is standing next to an opening.

135
00:09:40,999 --> 00:09:46,255
Every one of us is responsible not to let the enemy approach us, from that opening,

136
00:09:46,295 --> 00:09:51,835
 whether the enemy is Shaytan(شيطان), or the enemy is kuffar(كفار), whatever the enemy is.

137
00:09:52,369 --> 00:09:59,043
You don't want to be the one, who opens the door for the enemy to come through

138
00:09:59,518 --> 00:10:04,154
and every one of us has a responsibility and we need to take that responsibility seriously

139
00:10:04,566 --> 00:10:08,972
and your responsibility, depends on the gifts that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given you.

140
00:10:09,706 --> 00:10:13,441
So, if Allahعَزّوجَلّ has gifted you with knowledge,

141
00:10:14,186 --> 00:10:17,298
then you want to make sure that you are responsible.

142
00:10:17,503 --> 00:10:20,284
If Allahعَزّوجَلّ has gifted you with physical strength,

143
00:10:20,666 --> 00:10:22,859
you want to take care of that responsibility.

144
00:10:23,072 --> 00:10:27,208
If Allahعَزّوجَلّ has blessed you with wealth,

145
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:29,323
you want to make sure that you are responsible

146
00:10:29,363 --> 00:10:35,117
and you don't allow Shaytan(شيطان) to attack us, through your gate and that is by withholding your money.

147
00:10:36,609 --> 00:10:40,787
So, we ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us understand what our responsibilities are

148
00:10:40,827 --> 00:10:42,922
and fulfill them accordingly.

149
00:10:43,653 --> 00:10:47,946
During this Ghazwa(غزوة) an interesting conversation happened between Jabir Bin Abdullah رضي الله عنه

150
00:10:48,222 --> 00:10:51,775
and Rasool Allah ﷺ, we'll go through it.

151
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:56,220
Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله), was riding a feeble weak camel,

152
00:10:56,474 --> 00:11:01,657
and his comrades were getting ahead of him, so Rasool Allah ﷺ approaches him and said;

153
00:11:02,156 --> 00:11:03,272
What's wrong Jabir(جابر).?

154
00:11:03,636 --> 00:11:04,245
 So, he said;

155
00:11:04,310 --> 00:11:07,796
O Messenger of Allah, this camel of mine is slowing me down.

156
00:11:08,274 --> 00:11:10,201
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, make it kneel.

157
00:11:10,697 --> 00:11:13,226
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ also made his camel kneel

158
00:11:13,661 --> 00:11:16,588
and Rasool Allah dismounts and he tells Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله),

159
00:11:16,991 --> 00:11:22,358
Give me that stick of yours or get one for me from a tree.

160
00:11:23,116 --> 00:11:24,819
So, Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله) gives him the stick.

161
00:11:25,189 --> 00:11:29,335
Rasool Allah ﷺ prodded the camel, with that stick.

162
00:11:30,341 --> 00:11:33,417
And then he told Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله) mount up.

163
00:11:33,797 --> 00:11:35,592
Jabir(جابر) mounts the camel and he said;

164
00:11:36,021 --> 00:11:41,419
My weak Camel was now competing with the fast camel of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

165
00:11:42,431 --> 00:11:45,093
So this is a miracle of Rasool Allah ﷺ that occurred in this Gazwah(غزوة).

166
00:11:45,736 --> 00:11:48,555
By just placing or prodding the camel with that stick.

167
00:11:48,615 --> 00:11:51,670
Now, it suddenly became vigorous and strong.

168
00:11:52,353 --> 00:11:55,916
And then Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله) was conversing with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

169
00:11:55,956 --> 00:11:58,419
they were talking, so Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

170
00:11:58,947 --> 00:12:01,283
Would you sell me this Camel of yours, Jabir(جابر).

171
00:12:01,845 --> 00:12:04,410
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ likes to Camel and he wants to buy it.

172
00:12:04,684 --> 00:12:06,928
Jabir Bin Abdullah(جابر بن عبدالله) said: I'll just give it to you.

173
00:12:07,671 --> 00:12:10,268
I mean, the reason why it's fast now is because of you.

174
00:12:10,308 --> 00:12:12,885
I'll just give it up, or I'll give it to you.

175
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,996
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No,

176
00:12:15,210 --> 00:12:17,076
I want to buy it, just sell it to me.

177
00:12:17,839 --> 00:12:19,465
Jabir(جابر) said: Make me an offer.

178
00:12:20,073 --> 00:12:22,472
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: One Dirham(درهم).

179
