00:25:15,466 --> 00:25:17,581
if you'll refuse than we'll fight.

389
00:25:17,872 --> 00:25:19,404
if they are Mushrikeen(مشركين) then.

390
00:25:19,549 --> 00:25:20,909
Number one, you become Muslim,

391
00:25:20,989 --> 00:25:22,346
if you refuse than we'll fight.

392
00:25:22,832 --> 00:25:25,466
And they're given three days to make up their mind,

393
00:25:25,490 --> 00:25:28,699
not giving years and years of continuous Da'wah(دعوة),

394
00:25:28,995 --> 00:25:31,723
and it's only three days that is the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

395
00:25:31,761 --> 00:25:34,262
and that was the way of the Khulafaa(خلفآء) after him.

396
00:25:34,770 --> 00:25:37,837
But here they weren't even given a moment to think about it.

397
00:25:37,877 --> 00:25:39,659
Why? Because Da'wah(دعوة) has already reached them.

398
00:25:40,014 --> 00:25:42,093
They live in the Arabia, they already know about Islam,

399
00:25:42,149 --> 00:25:44,824
they heard about Rasool Allah ﷺ too, so it's not something new.

400
00:25:45,059 --> 00:25:46,328
 So, they were ambushed.

401
00:25:47,132 --> 00:25:49,408
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبد الله بن عمر) said and this is in Bukhari(البخاري)

402
00:25:49,597 --> 00:25:53,010
فَأَغَارَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَهُمْ غَارُّونَ، وَأَنْعَامُهُمْ تُسْقَى عَلَى المَاءِ

403
00:25:53,307 --> 00:25:57,970
 فَقَتَلَ مُقَاتِلَتَهُمْ ، وَسَبَى ذَرَارِيَّهُمْ ، وَأَصَابَ يَوْمَئِذٍ جُوَيْرِيَةَ بِنْتِ حَارِثْ

404
00:25:58,229 --> 00:26:00,314
He attacked them, while they were unaware,

405
00:26:00,549 --> 00:26:03,586
 while their livestock were drinking water,

406
00:26:03,883 --> 00:26:08,937
so he killed some of their men and he has taken their families as slaves,

407
00:26:09,016 --> 00:26:10,048
 this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

408
00:26:11,186 --> 00:26:13,231
They would use the battle cries.

409
00:26:13,567 --> 00:26:16,060
So, in this battle, their battle cry was,

410
00:26:16,107 --> 00:26:17,845
يا منصورامت امت

411
00:26:17,933 --> 00:26:19,861
 which means, O conquer Kill, kill.

412
00:26:20,224 --> 00:26:21,702
That was their battle cry.

413
00:26:22,203 --> 00:26:26,094
Also, alot of Fiqh(فقه) was learned during the Ghazawaat(غزوات).

414
00:26:26,406 --> 00:26:30,510
So, this is another objective that was served by traveling with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

415
00:26:30,550 --> 00:26:31,812
they learned the Fiqh(فقه) from him.

416
00:26:32,190 --> 00:26:34,075
So, during the Ghazwa(غزوة) of Bannu Mustallaq(بنو مصطلق),

417
00:26:34,582 --> 00:26:38,054
the ruling of Tayammum(تيمم) was revealed in Qur'an.

418
00:26:38,521 --> 00:26:42,935
And the Fiqh(فقه) of it was learned from Rasool Allah ﷺ, right then and there.

419
00:26:43,703 --> 00:26:47,837
Also another, for example, show you how they would learn Fiqh(فقه) in this Ghazwa(غزوة),

420
00:26:48,620 --> 00:26:50,941
in Bukhari(بخاري) Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابوسعيد الخدري) said;

421
00:26:51,378 --> 00:26:55,560
We went forth with the Messenger of Allah, on the expedition to Bannu Mustallaq(بنومصطلق),

422
00:26:55,922 --> 00:26:58,097
we took many of the Bedouin captive.

423
00:26:58,408 --> 00:27:02,695
And we desired the women because celibacy was very hard on us.

424
00:27:03,358 --> 00:27:05,152
We like the practice of Azal(عزل),

425
00:27:05,461 --> 00:27:12,327
Azal(عزل) is the interruption of sexual intercourse by the male withdrawal before ejaculation,

426
00:27:12,367 --> 00:27:15,134
so we can say that it's a form of contraceptive.

427
00:27:15,515 --> 00:27:18,154
So, he says: We liked the practice of Azal(عزل)

428
00:27:18,257 --> 00:27:22,566
but wondered whether we should do this without asking the Messenger of Allah.

429
00:27:22,864 --> 00:27:24,289
So, we asked them about it, he said;

430
00:27:24,369 --> 00:27:30,463
There is no difference in you doing that, for any soul that is going to exist till Judgment Day, will so exist.

431
00:27:31,253 --> 00:27:34,591
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said that it wouldn't make a difference.

432
00:27:34,940 --> 00:27:37,349
If you do that or not because Allah has already made Qadar(قدر),

433
00:27:37,389 --> 00:27:40,452
has already ordained every soul that will be created.

434
00:27:40,813 --> 00:27:45,810
Now some Ulema(علماء), use this Hadith(حديث) as evidence that contraceptives are allowed.

435
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:47,807
Now I'm not going to get into the Fiqh(فقه) of it.

436
00:27:47,905 --> 00:27:51,293
 I mean, for example the among our classical scholars

437
00:27:51,333 --> 00:27:55,199
there's a difference of opinion on whether it is Mubah(مباح) or Makrooh(مكروه) or Haram(حرام).

438
00:27:55,691 --> 00:27:58,658
And then it was also, there's a difference of opinion

439
00:27:58,698 --> 00:28:04,507
on whether this is relating to a free woman, a wife, or a slave girl.

440
00:28:05,091 --> 00:28:08,991
Now the reason, why they want to practice Azal(عزل) here

441
00:28:09,420 --> 00:28:17,177
is because, if a man owns a slave woman, and she becomes pregnant, and has a child from him.

442
00:28:17,407 --> 00:28:18,923
 Then he cannot sell her.

443
00:28:19,605 --> 00:28:22,566
So, she remains with him, now because of the children,

444
00:28:23,054 --> 00:28:24,594
and she is called Ummo Walad(ام ولد),

445
00:28:24,726 --> 00:28:28,164
a mother of children and she's becomes almost like his wife.

446
00:28:28,852 --> 00:28:31,463
However, if they are practicing Azal(عزل).

447
00:28:31,879 --> 00:28:35,618
Then, they would have sexual relations with these women

448
00:28:35,648 --> 00:28:41,001
but then they can sell them, so that's why they were asking Rasool Allah ﷺ, about it.

449
00:28:42,170 --> 00:28:49,420
Let me narrate here, what Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said about an event that happened

450
00:28:49,929 --> 00:28:52,027
during the Ghazwa(غزوة), of Bannu Bannu Mustallaq(بنومصطلق).

451
00:28:52,758 --> 00:28:54,665
This is by Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق)

452
00:28:54,718 --> 00:29:02,266
but it's also narrated by Al-Hakim(الحاكم) and it is Jayyid(جيد) Sanad(سند), with good, chain of narrators.

453
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:04,370
 Ayesha رضي الله عنها said;

454
00:29:04,708 --> 00:29:09,354
When the Messenger of Allah, distributed the captives taken from Bannu Mustallaq(بنومصطلق),

455
00:29:09,487 --> 00:29:14,435
Jawairiyyah(جويريه), daughter of Al-Haris(الحارث) was awarded to Thabit Bin Qais Bin Shammas(ثابت بن قيس بن شماس),

456
00:29:14,666 --> 00:29:19,519
there was one woman, who was taken captive and she's the daughter of the head of the tribe, her name is Jawairiyyah(جويريه),

457
00:29:20,442 --> 00:29:22,040
and she wrote Mukataba(مكاتبه).

458
00:29:22,080 --> 00:29:22,828
Ayesha(عائشه) said;

459
00:29:22,977 --> 00:29:26,709
She made the Mukataba(مكاتبه) with Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس بن شماس).

460
00:29:27,011 --> 00:29:32,461
Now Mukataba(مكاتبه) is a contract between the master and the slave,

461
00:29:33,130 --> 00:29:39,995
which would allow the slave to be emancipated, to be freed by paying a certain amount of money.

462
00:29:40,637 --> 00:29:46,076
So, Islam does not make slavery, a perpetual thing on a person it's not permanent.

463
00:29:46,573 --> 00:29:53,152
A person who desires to be free, does have that right and can be free.

464
00:29:53,478 --> 00:29:57,646
By the way, and whenever we talk about slavery in Islam.

465
00:29:57,967 --> 00:30:03,630
It's a completely different thing, compared to the slavery that existed in Europe or America.

466
00:30:04,005 --> 00:30:08,340
So, one should not compare the two or consider them equal, it's different.

467
00:30:08,403 --> 00:30:13,046
Slavery in Islam is different, slaves had rights, they were treated well,

468
00:30:13,418 --> 00:30:17,275
that they were respected, they became scholars, they became kings.

469
00:30:17,605 --> 00:30:21,454
For example, many of this these slaves became scholars among the Tabieen(تابعين),

470
00:30:21,807 --> 00:30:25,426
and some of them even ruled and became kings.

471
00:30:25,612 --> 00:30:28,830
Like with Dulatel Mumalik(دولةالمماليك), this was an entire dynasty

472
00:30:29,005 --> 00:30:31,570
that was called the dynasty of the slaves.

473
00:30:31,824 --> 00:30:33,520
These were slaves, who became kings.

474
00:30:34,050 --> 00:30:38,840
That's something unimaginable, in the western institution of slavery.

475
00:30:39,365 --> 00:30:44,031
Plus slavery among Muslims, had nothing to do with ethnicity.

476
00:30:44,822 --> 00:30:47,160
Unlike in the west for example in America

477
00:30:47,508 --> 00:30:50,750
slavery was only blacks can be slaves,

478
00:30:50,964 --> 00:30:55,851
and only whites can be the owners of the slaves.

479
00:30:56,367 --> 00:30:58,240
That's not the case in Islam,

480
00:30:58,535 --> 00:31:02,500
a slave could be white, could be black, could be Arab,

481
00:31:02,843 --> 00:31:06,031
over here Rasool Allah ﷺ enslaved the people who are Arab.

482
00:31:06,658 --> 00:31:09,894
And we know that in the wars between the Muslims and the Roman Empire's,

483
00:31:09,918 --> 00:31:13,213
their prisoners of war were taken as slaves and these are European.

484
00:31:13,585 --> 00:31:16,864
And you also had African slaves, such as Bilal(بلال)

485
00:31:17,145 --> 00:31:19,342
and Salman Farisi(سلمان فارسي), he was a Persian slave.

486
00:31:19,807 --> 00:31:22,176
So it had nothing to do with ethnicity,

487
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:26,448
it's unlike the western system of slavery, which is nothing more than racism.

488
00:31:27,503 --> 00:31:29,578
So, anyway she made a Mukataba(مكاتبه)

489
00:31:29,618 --> 00:31:36,530
and this is something that shows you that if a slave isn't pleased with that profession

490
00:31:36,570 --> 00:31:39,122
 because that was really what it was, in Islam, it was a profession.

491
00:31:39,651 --> 00:31:41,674
Then they have the right to change it.

492
00:31:42,163 --> 00:31:44,068
And that is what Jawairiyyah(جويريه) wanted to do,

493
00:31:44,108 --> 00:31:46,678
she made the Mukataba(مكاتبه) between her and her master.

494
00:31:47,420 --> 00:31:51,415
Ayesha(عائشه) said: She was a very sweet and attractive woman.

495
00:31:51,904 --> 00:31:54,194
Every man who saw her, fell for her.

496
00:31:54,787 --> 00:31:59,671
She came to the messenger of Allah, to ask him help, in preparing the document,

497
00:32:00,159 --> 00:32:03,913
 and I swear, as soon as I saw her at the door of my room,

498
00:32:04,290 --> 00:32:08,304
I disliked her and recognize that he would see in her, what I did.

499
00:32:08,714 --> 00:32:10,632
Ayesha(عائشه) was saying that she felt jealous

500
00:32:10,845 --> 00:32:12,652
because Jawairiyyah(جويريه) was beautiful

501
00:32:12,692 --> 00:32:17,739
and Ayesha(عائشه) was worried if Rasool Allah ﷺ sees her, he might want to get married to her.

502
00:32:18,551 --> 00:32:20,638
When she went into him, she said;

503
00:32:20,701 --> 00:32:27,010
 Messenger of Allah, I am Jawairiyyah(جويريه), a daughter of Al-Haris Bin Abu Zarar(الحارث بن ابو ضرار), the leader of his people.

504
00:32:27,304 --> 00:32:29,391
You can see what my plight is now,

505
00:32:29,553 --> 00:32:32,962
I have fallen to the lot of Thabit Bin Qais Bin Shammas(ثابت بن قيس بن شماس),

506
00:32:33,289 --> 00:32:36,444
and I've prepared the deed, awarding myself to him.

507
00:32:36,753 --> 00:32:39,547
I've come to ask your help in writing it.

508
00:32:40,050 --> 00:32:42,948
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Would you prefer better.

509
00:32:43,253 --> 00:32:45,190
She said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah?

510
00:32:45,557 --> 00:32:50,632
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I will take responsibility for your deed myself and marry you.

511
00:32:51,382 --> 00:32:54,466
She replied; Yes, Messenger of Allah, I agree.

512
00:32:55,202 --> 00:32:57,180
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ married Jawairiyyah(جويريه),

513
00:32:57,460 --> 00:32:59,455
and he paid her ransom.

514
00:33:00,104 --> 00:33:05,193
Now the news spread that Rasool Allah ﷺ had married Jawairiyyah(جويريه) and the people said;

515
00:33:05,793 --> 00:33:11,487
Then they, meaning our captives are relatives of Rasool Allah ﷺ, so they released the captives.

516
00:33:12,106 --> 00:33:14,648
Why.? Because Jawairiyyah(جويريه) is now the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

517
00:33:14,688 --> 00:33:18,369
they didn't want her relatives to be slaves, so they freed them.

518
00:33:18,772 --> 00:33:22,492
Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said: And so by his marriage to her,

519
00:33:22,745 --> 00:33:26,604
he released 100 of her relatives from Bannu Mustallaq(بنومصطلق),

520
00:33:26,712 --> 00:33:31,045
I know, no woman who brought greater blessings to her people than she.

521
00:33:31,272 --> 00:33:35,789
So, Jawairiyyah(جويريه) was a blessing on her people, they were freed, because of her.

522
00:33:36,896 --> 00:33:39,198
Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) had a servant,

523
00:33:39,845 --> 00:33:46,539
and his servant was Mohajer(مهاجر), and they were next to this well, fetching water.

524
00:33:47,047 --> 00:33:52,705
And this servant of Umar(عمر), got into a fight with one on of Al-Ansaar(الانصار)

525
00:33:53,371 --> 00:33:57,339
 because of the crowding at this well.

526
00:33:57,895 --> 00:34:04,822
They got in each other's way and, you know, one word, next word, and then they had a dispute and a fight.

527
00:34:05,828 --> 00:34:07,215
So, the Ansaari(انصاري) said;

528
00:34:07,255 --> 00:34:08,262
 يا لِلْأنْصَارْ

529
00:34:08,352 --> 00:34:12,857
He was calling the Ansaar(انصار) to come and gang up, against this Mohajeri(مهاجري)

530
00:34:12,897 --> 00:34:14,469
 and the Mohajeri(مهاجري) did the same.

531
00:34:15,109 --> 00:34:21,109
So, a fight was almost going to break out between the two parties, of Muslims, Al-Muhajiroon(المهاجرون) and Al-Ansaar(الانصار),

532
00:34:21,149 --> 00:34:24,277
until Rasool Allah ﷺ came in and mediated between them.

533
00:34:24,470 --> 00:34:26,465
Rasool Allah ﷺ would not allow such things to happen,

534
00:34:26,505 --> 00:34:31,879
he would immediately be on the spot, come in and stop such fittan(فتن)

535
00:34:32,485 --> 00:34:35,500
and when they're in the bud, he will not allow them to grow.

536
00:34:36,196 --> 00:34:38,708
That's an important aspect of leadership,

537
00:34:39,136 --> 00:34:46,041
not to be unaware, and neglectful of Fittan(فتن) that could end up, breaking up the Jama'ah(جماعة).

538
00:34:46,599 --> 00:34:50,069
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ steps in immediately and he stops it early,

539
00:34:50,459 --> 00:34:52,093
before it gets out of control.

540
00:34:52,669 --> 00:34:57,242
Now the news reaches to Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَي), the head of Al-Munafiqoon(المنافقون).

541
00:34:57,682 --> 00:35:01,889
And he said: Did they really cause this.?

542
00:35:02,424 --> 00:35:06,100
They challenge us, and outnumber us, in our own land.

543
00:35:06,538 --> 00:35:11,758
I swear by Allah, the old Maxim well applies to us on these Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) ruffians,

544
00:35:12,044 --> 00:35:15,406
fatten your dog, and you, it will eat.

545
00:35:15,946 --> 00:35:21,062
Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَي) is saying we brought in these Mohajiroon(مهاجرون) into our land

546
00:35:21,102 --> 00:35:22,740
and look at what he said about them.

547
00:35:22,835 --> 00:35:25,484
 It's like, we fatten them and then they eat us.

548
00:35:25,766 --> 00:35:28,805
I mean, he using this maxim, fatten your dog and it will eat you.

549
00:35:29,897 --> 00:35:34,460
I swear, when we return to Madina, the stronger will drive out the weaker

550
00:35:34,500 --> 00:35:40,787
and in Arabic, It is; Al-Azz(العز), the more honorable or the stronger.

551
00:35:41,004 --> 00:35:43,668
Both are correct meaning translations to the word Al-Azz(العز),

552
00:35:43,848 --> 00:35:49,282
the stronger or the more honorable will drive out the weaker or the humble.

553
00:35:50,321 --> 00:35:52,119
See what you have done to yourselves,

554
00:35:52,522 --> 00:35:56,774
you let them settle among you and shared your property with them.

555
00:35:57,066 --> 00:36:00,111
I swear if you had kept what you owned from them,

556
00:36:00,308 --> 00:36:01,756
they would have gone somewhere else.

557
00:36:03,271 --> 00:36:05,756
This Nifaaq(نفاق) is coming out of his mouth,

558
00:36:07,006 --> 00:36:09,274
a young Sahabi(صحابي), his name is Zaid Bin Arqam(زيد بن ارقم),

559
00:36:09,953 --> 00:36:12,253
he heard what Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن اُبَي) said.

560
00:36:12,678 --> 00:36:15,242
So he goes and conveys the news to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

561
00:36:16,316 --> 00:36:22,047
Some men from Al-Ansaar(الانصار), who were present told Rasool Allah ﷺ

562
00:36:22,689 --> 00:36:27,389
perhaps the lad mistook what was said or did not memorize it correctly.

563
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:31,481
So, they were defending Abdullah Bin Obaey(عبد الله بن ابي)

564
00:36:31,521 --> 00:36:33,862
they said probably this young boy didn't hear it right.

565
00:36:34,233 --> 00:36:38,052
Umar(عمر) said: Let me go and execute this Munafiq(منافق).

566
00:36:38,493 --> 00:36:41,906
Umar(عمر) doesn't play around, Let me go and execute him.

567
00:36:43,410 --> 00:36:48,627
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: How would it be Umar(عمر), to have people say,

568
00:36:48,667 --> 00:36:51,873
that Muhammad(محمد) kills his own companions.

569
00:36:52,135 --> 00:36:54,762
No, give orders to leave instead.

570
00:36:55,344 --> 00:36:58,886
And we're going to come back to the statement by Rasool Allah ﷺ because there's Hikmah(حكمة)

571
00:36:59,546 --> 00:37:01,339
that we can learn from this statement.

572
00:37:02,494 --> 00:37:09,890
Usaid رضي الله عنه Bin Khuzair(بن خضير), one of Al-Ansaar(الانصار), is from the people of Abdullah Bin Obaey(عبد الله بن ابي).

573
00:37:10,303 --> 00:37:13,612
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Didn't you hear what your friend said. He said;

574
00:37:14,030 --> 00:37:14,827
which friend.?

575
00:37:15,177 --> 00:37:17,359
He said: Abdullah Bin Obaey(عبد الله بن ابي), what did he say.?

576
00:37:17,811 --> 00:37:20,351
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: What he said.

577
00:37:20,716 --> 00:37:22,248
 Usaid رضي الله عنه said;

578
00:37:22,571 --> 00:37:26,997
Well, I swear by Allah, messenger of Allah you will drive him out, if you wish.

579
00:37:27,337 --> 00:37:29,942
He is certainly the weak one and you are the strong.

580
00:37:30,815 --> 00:37:33,241
And then he said, Be kind to him, O messenger of Allah,

581
00:37:33,582 --> 00:37:41,293
I swear Allah brought you to us, while his people were stringing pearls, with which to make a crown for him.

582
00:37:41,504 --> 00:37:44,730
And so he considers that you have robbed him his kingdom.

583
00:37:45,165 --> 00:37:49,142
And this is a problem with the people of authority and the people who have money.

584
00:37:50,329 --> 00:37:54,520
